H2: Frequently Asked Questions
H3: What's included in a forex turnkey solution?
 A trading platform, CRM, liquidity connectivity, hosting, website, client portal, payment integration, KYC integration, API access and ongoing support, all configured to work together.
H3: Can I keep some of my existing tools?
 Yes. If you already have a CRM, liquidity provider or payment provider you want to keep, we can build the rest of the stack around it, provided it supports integration.
H3: Does a turnkey solution include a broker licence?
 No. We provide technology. Licensing and regulatory requirements vary by jurisdiction and need to be handled with legal and compliance advisors.
H3: Should I choose MT5 or MT4?
 Most new brokers choose MT5 for its multi-asset support and long-term outlook. We'll recommend MT4 only if your target clients specifically rely on it.
H3: White label or grey label?
 Both can be delivered as part of a turnkey setup. Grey label suits leaner launches. White label generally gives you greater control and suits brokers planning for growth.
H3: How long does a turnkey setup take?
 It depends on scope and on how quickly liquidity and payment providers onboard you. We'll give you a realistic timeline after discovery rather than a number designed to win the deal.
H3: How is pricing structured?
 Pricing depends on your platform model, integrations, number of providers and the scope of your website and portal. You'll receive a clear breakdown after the consultation, including one-off and recurring costs.
H3: What happens after launch?
 We stay on as your technology partner, handling monitoring, maintenance, changes and support as your brokerage grows.
H3: Can I add products later?
 Yes. Mobile trading apps, web trading, PAMM and MAM, new payment methods and additional liquidity providers can all be added to the same stack.
